# The issue-55 OSS defect corpus is content-addressed: each committed
# snapshot must hash to the git blob SHA and byte count recorded in
# docs/measurements/issue-55/corpus/manifest.json. Git must therefore never
# perform line-ending normalization (LF <-> CRLF) on these files, otherwise
# the byte-fidelity gate (Pipeline.Validate / CorpusIntegrityTests) fails on
# platforms where checkout normalization applies (windows-latest runners
# default to core.autocrlf=true).
docs/measurements/issue-55/corpus/files/** -text
